(- Access Route      : Right Radial Artery Approach) '
(- Stents Deployed   :) '
(  * Resolute Onyx Zotarolimus-Eluting Stent \(3.0 x 24 mm\) deployed in Mid-LAD) '
(  * Promus Premier Everolimus-Eluting Stent \(2.75 x 18 mm\) deployed in Proximal LCx) '
(- Angiographic Result: Excellent final angiographic result with TIMI III distal flow.) '
(                      Zero residual stenosis, no dissection, no thrombus.) '
T*
(HOSPITAL COURSE & CLINICAL SUMMARY:) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(Patient presented with retrosternal chest discomfort, diaphoresis, and exertional) '
(dyspnea. Initial Troponin-I was elevated \(1.82 ng/mL\). Coronary angiography revealed) '
(90% stenosis in mid-LAD and 80% stenosis in proximal LCx. Successful primary stenting) '
(was executed without complications. Radial sheath was removed with TR-Band compression) '
(hemostasis. Post-procedure 48-hour continuous telemetry showed sinus rhythm with no) '
(ventricular ectopy. Echo showed preserved LVEF 52% with regional wall motion abnormality) '
(in anterior wall. Vitals prior to discharge: BP 124/78 mmHg, HR 68 bpm \(regular\),) '
(SpO2 98% on room air, Afebrile, radial puncture site clean with zero hematoma.) '
